// Test case 10 / 11: the data instance where the two groupings disagree.
// GRAMMAR.md section 3.3 uses exactly these relations.
//
//   A union B minus C   parses as (A union B) minus C  ->  {2}
//   A union (B minus C) would give                         {1,2}
//
// Run all three to see the grouping change the answer:
//   ra.py --db examples/case10.ra "A union B minus C"
//   ra.py --db examples/case10.ra "(A union B) minus C"
//   ra.py --db examples/case10.ra "A union (B minus C)"

A (x) = {
  1
}
B (x) = {
  2
}
C (x) = {
  1
}
